{{!--
    One Thread's Expiration Clock.

    ALWAYS A BAR, never pips — which is where it deliberately differs from the
    Consequence beside it. The Consequence mirrors the reading it stands under,
    because it is another count of the same situation; time is not the Thread's
    own arithmetic and does not take its shape. A deadline drawn as segments
    beside a Clock Thread's segments would read as more of the same number.

    IT COUNTS DOWN. Nobody counts up to a door closing, so the reading is what is
    LEFT — inverted once, by projectProgress, the same funnel every depleting
    Thread already passes through.

    THE LABEL IS THE CONTROL, as it is on the Consequence and for the same
    reason: the reading above this one ends in nothing, so a button parked after
    the number moved this row's number out of that column. "Time left" is the
    press.

    It is drawn whatever clock this rides, because GM fiat is possible on all
    three: what the setting decides is what ELSE moves it. It is also the one
    control on a Thread row that survives a shut gate, because a window closing
    on something you could not reach is exactly what a deadline on a locked
    Thread means.

    Parameters: `track` (the reading) and `threadId`.
--}}
<div class="rsr-expiry{{#if track.isExpired}} is-expired{{/if}}">
    {{#if track.canPush}}
    <button type="button" class="rsr-expiry-label" data-action="pushThread"
            name="push-expiry-{{threadId}}"
            data-thread-id="{{threadId}}" data-track="expiry"
            data-tooltip="{{localize 'RSR.editor.pushExpiryHint'}}">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-hourglass-half" inert></i>
        {{localize "RSR.thread.expiry"}}
    </button>
    {{else}}
    <span class="rsr-expiry-label">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-hourglass-half" inert></i>
        {{localize "RSR.thread.expiry"}}
    </span>
    {{/if}}

    <span class="rsr-bar">
        <span class="rsr-bar-fill" style="width: {{track.percent}}%"></span>
    </span>

    {{#if track.showValues}}
    <span class="rsr-bar-value">{{track.current}}<span class="rsr-of">/{{track.total}}</span></span>
    {{/if}}

    {{!-- The GM's own word for it — this Thread's, else the world's, else the
          built-in one. Already resolved in _prepareContext, so there is nothing
          to localize here and nothing to concatenate. --}}
    {{#if track.isExpired}}
    <span class="rsr-ready rsr-ready-expired">{{track.label}}</span>
    {{/if}}
</div>
